    "description": "Blank Audio Cassette Tape Lot  13 Tapes\nMixed Brands, 1980s-1990s\nTDK, Maxell, Realistic, Certron\nA diverse collection of thirteen blank audio cassette tapes featuring leading magnetic media brands from the late 20th century. This lot is notable for containing a high proportion of factory-sealed vintage stock, which remains highly sought after by analog recording enthusiasts for their specific sonic characteristics and period-correct aesthetics. The selection spans various formulations including standard Normal Bias and high-performance Chrome-equivalent tapes.\n9 Factory-Sealed tapes and 4 unsealed/opened tapes\nMix of 60-minute and 90-minute recording lengths\nIncludes Type I (Normal Bias) and Type II (Chrome/High Bias) formulations\nFeatures TDK D90, Maxell UR series, and Realistic Supertape HD-90\nCondition:\nNine tapes are factory sealed in original cellophane; several wrappers exhibit light shelf wear, minor corner scuffs, or remnants of vintage retail price stickers. Four tapes are unsealed and housed in standard clear protective cases; the recording status and internal J-card condition of these opened tapes have not been verified. Clear plastic cases on unsealed units show typical surface scuffing and light scratches from storage. Realistic Supertape and one Maxell XLII-S represent the Type II High-Bias media in this collection.\nPlease Read:\nAll items are donated and may exhibit signs of wear, including surface dirt, discoloration, scratches, and scuffs. Glassware and dishes may display color fading, crazing, or chips. Clothing items may have loose threads or fabric pilling. The full functionality of electrical items is not guaranteed. Purses may show wear on the bottom edges, corners, and handles. Jewelry metal content and stones have not been tested unless explicitly stated, and stones have not been individually inspected. Items sold in lots have not been counted or sorted and may contain small or damaged pieces. Returns are not accepted for these items.\nPlease carefully review photos and descriptions prior to bidding. If you have any questions or uncertainties, please contact us by opening a customer service ticket.",
